"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d95f41532fa95b219d06ae7cd361d7963aba5699d4a3dd7abc9072ec5ef73752","event_uuid":"9b4fb844-176b-40d6-8452-6ae6f78c1ab6","position":{"commit_sha":"70021fb826cdc73222b7e6526e8fd3be1725a04f","position":"1785915265198854001-9b4fb844-176b-40d6-8452-6ae6f78c1ab6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0ea620eb2b7093aa11a3bde4d710a005c80c5e77d863538aedf5e15a1a031eb0","event_uuid":"bd008a0e-5895-465a-ae0f-9552490dd05b","position":{"commit_sha":"41f9179d799939665793dc2b1d9efb8188f5f1b6","position":"1785915517806419001-bd008a0e-5895-465a-ae0f-9552490dd05b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-222_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"4cf58ecd-8513-4de1-a7b6-62b672e02919","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 1427 pushed: guards applied to all 11 enumerated steps in _build-and-test.yml (9) and gerrit-verify.yaml golden-path (2), plus the structural guard the AC asks for. Full detail in the follow-up comment. Awaiting Verified +1.","timestamp":1785915182076469001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Fixed — Gerrit change 1427\n\n**Root cause (re-verified, not re-derived).** Gerrit's Verified lane takes the workflow\nDEFINITION from the target branch but checks out the CHANGE'S tree, so a gate step added on\nmain runs against open changes whose base predates its script. Reproduced directly: running\n`python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` and `python scripts/check_config_reads.py` in a\ndirectory without them exits **2** with `can't open file ... [Errno 2]` — a hard CI failure\nindistinguishable from a real gate violation.\n\n**Guarded — 11 steps, exactly the set this ticket enumerated.**\n\n`_build-and-test.yml` (9): Verified-gate parity, comment-hygiene, Env-var registry drift,\nDocs-index completeness, README quickstart golden-path, CLI-reference drift, MCP-reference\ndrift, server.json env-contract drift, Config-read.\n\n`gerrit-verify.yaml` golden-path (2): README quickstart golden-path, End-to-end CLI probe.\n\nEach gains the same early-return guard the raw-git-write gate uses. **Everything below each\nguard is byte-for-byte unchanged.** The only deletions in the whole diff are five inline\n`run:` lines becoming block form, with their command preserved verbatim — a reviewer can\nconfirm no gate was weakened by reading the deletion list alone.\n\n**Both tree cases proven per step** (`tests/unit/test_gate_step_tree_skew.py`, which lifts\neach step's real `run:` body out of the live YAML and executes it under the shell GitHub\nActions would use):\n\n- *absent script* — exit 0, a log line naming the tree-skew cause, no `::error::` annotation;\n- *present script* — a stub that records that it ran and then exits non-zero: the step must\n  both invoke it and still fail the build. Enforcement intact.\n\n**RED to GREEN.** 33 failures before the fix (11 structural + 22 behavioral), 53 passed after.\nMutation-checked in both directions: removing one guard returns its 3 tests to RED; making a\nguard always-skip returns the present-script test to RED, so the tests catch weakening too.\n\n**The structural guard landed.** It walks both patchset-lane workflows, selects only the jobs\nthat use `checkout-gerrit-change-action` (the ones that check out the change's tree), and\nfails on any step running a repo script without an if-present guard. The ee2a convention no\nlonger depends on an author remembering the note — this prevents the 12th instance, not just\nthe 11. Scoping needed no design decision: the vote job's `normalize_ci_conclusion` step is\ncorrectly excluded because it deliberately sparse-checks-out its script from the trusted\ndefault branch, not the patchset. A vacuity assertion guards the detector itself.\n\n**Scope and safety.** No new dependency, no pre-existing test touched, no enforcement path\naltered. Full unit suite 3923 passed / 0 failed; lint + mypy clean; zizmor findings identical\npre- and post-change (22, none new); actionlint clean.\n\nNot closing until Verified +1 and merged.","timestamp":1785915227537625001}],"created_at":1785911752713508001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"671deaa6-7b35-40a8-8da4-25de68fd89c3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"7e90-233b-3ee9-4f14"}],"description":"## The defect\n\nBug 7e90-233b-3ee9-4f14 fixed the `Git version floor gate` step, which hard-failed every\nchange branched before its data file landed. The same class of defect is still live in\n`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` on OTHER gate steps that run a repo script with no\nif-present guard.\n\nThe workflow's own \"Definition-vs-tree skew guard (ticket ee2a)\" note states the rule\nverbatim: a gate step that runs a repo script must skip (with a log line) when the script is\nabsent from the checked-out tree. Gerrit's Verified lane takes the workflow DEFINITION from\nthe target branch but checks out the CHANGE'S tree, so a step added on main runs against\nopen changes whose base predates its script.\n\n## Unguarded gate steps (swept from the parsed workflow YAML)\n\nIn `_build-and-test.yml`, which BOTH the Gerrit Verified lane and branch CI run:\n\n| step | script | script first added |\n|---|---|---|\n| `comment-hygiene gate` | `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` | 2026-08-03 |\n| `Config-read gate` | `scripts/check_config_reads.py` | 2026-08-02 |\n| `Verified-gate parity gate` | `scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` | 2026-07-19 |\n| `Env-var registry drift gate` | `scripts/gen_env_registry.py` | 2026-07-08 |\n| `Docs-index completeness gate` | `scripts/check_docs_index.py` | 2026-07-11 |\n| `README quickstart golden-path gate` | `scripts/check_readme_quickstart.py` | 2026-07-11 |\n| `CLI-reference drift gate` | `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` | 2026-07-11 |\n| `MCP-reference drift gate` | `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py` | 2026-07-11 |\n| `server.json env-contract drift gate` | `scripts/check_server_manifest.py` | 2026-07-04 |\n\nThe two 2026-08-02/03 scripts are the LIVE exposure -- open changes branched before those\ndates exist today. The older ones are the same latent class and should be guarded for\nuniformity, so the next reader does not have to re-derive which are safe.\n\n`gerrit-verify.yaml`'s `golden-path` job also checks out the Gerrit patchset and runs\n`scripts/check_readme_quickstart.py` and `scripts/probe_rebar.py` unguarded -- same class,\nsame lane.\n\n## Confirmed empirically\n\nRunning each unguarded step's command in a directory without the script exits 2 with\n`can't open file '.../scripts/<name>.py': [Errno 2] No such file or directory` -- a hard CI\nfailure indistinguishable from a real gate violation, which is exactly what produced the\nfalse Verified -1 in 7e90.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Every gate step in `_build-and-test.yml` that runs a repo script carries the ee2a\n      if-present guard, skipping with a log line naming the tree-skew cause.\n- [x] The `golden-path` job in `gerrit-verify.yaml` is guarded the same way.\n- [x] A genuine gate violation still fails when the script IS present -- no gate is weakened.\n- [x] A test (mirroring `tests/unit/test_git_floor_gate_tree_skew.py`) executes each guarded\n      step against a tree lacking the script and asserts it exits 0 without an `::error::`.\n- [x] Consider a structural guard: a check that FAILS when a step in the Verified lane runs a\n      repo script without the if-present guard, so the convention stops depending on authors\n      remembering the ee2a note.\n\n## Provenance\n\nFound by the Step 7 sibling sweep while fixing bug 7e90-233b-3ee9-4f14.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"add the ee2a if-present guard to the 9 unguarded gate steps that run a repo script"},{"path":".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","reason":"add the same guard to the golden-path job (check_readme_quickstart.py, probe_rebar.py)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_step_tree_skew.py","reason":"new: execute each guarded step against absent-script and present-script trees; structural guard that fails on any unguarded repo-script step"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a61e11cf-5c13-459a-8103-53b991bc09f8","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1909-c1a7-9f20-440f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Other CI gate steps still hard-fail on the definition-vs-tree skew","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c35b1ec0-49bc-4909-bd37-77123405d41d","671deaa6-7b35-40a8-8da4-25de68fd89c3","d55b5d3b-6d22-4788-8c6b-136442a4e488","4214e323-62d3-4895-8bcf-b862b9b28763","a61e11cf-5c13-459a-8103-53b991bc09f8","ce2366b0-f2a4-4b37-890e-d63d4b2898ef","72bfa1e2-feb1-49d9-a600-94c8445071d0","8cce446a-3f60-43ef-aa23-1dd341d8e572","9b4fb844-176b-40d6-8452-6ae6f78c1ab6","bd008a0e-5895-465a-ae0f-9552490dd05b"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785915517806419002,"uuid":"189787db-8b8c-4d1e-a5b0-ca60c0cfe88f"}